{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/staffdetails"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/staffDetails","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffDetails"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV","text":"MXLStaffDetails","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<staff-details>"},{"type":"text","text":" elements."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"staffDetails","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffDetails"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStaffDetails","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAttributesV12staffDetailsSayAA08MXLStaffE0VGvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes/staffDetails":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes\/staffDetails","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes\/staffdetails","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"staffDetails","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"staffDetails","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAttributes","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffDetails"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}